  "question": {
    "text": "A particle has two velocities of equal magnitude inclined to each other at an angle $\\theta$. If one of them is halved, the angle between the other and the original resultant velocity is bisected by the new resultant. Then $\\theta$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$90^{\\circ}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$120^{\\circ}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$45^{\\circ}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$60^{\\circ}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0261_ff5c4c0aaad6.png\"><br>\n$\\tan \\frac{\\theta}{4}=\\frac{\\frac{u}{2} \\sin \\theta}{u+\\frac{u}{2} \\cos \\theta}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\sin \\frac{\\theta}{4}+\\frac{1}{2} \\sin \\frac{\\theta}{4} \\cos \\theta=\\frac{1}{2} \\sin \\theta \\cos \\frac{\\theta}{4}$\n$\\therefore 2 \\sin \\frac{\\theta}{4}=\\sin \\frac{3 \\theta}{4}=3 \\sin \\frac{\\theta}{4}-4 \\sin ^3 \\frac{\\theta}{4}$\n$\\therefore \\sin ^2 \\frac{\\theta}{4}=\\frac{1}{4} \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\theta}{4}=30^{\\circ}$ or $\\theta=120^{\\circ}$"
  }
